  "comment": "THE PROTAGONIST, from the user's own pose sheet (art/player/source/hero-sheet.png) — made by `npm run assets:animate` from art/player/source/hero.poses.json (which drawing is which), hero.rig.json (where the parts of each drawing are) and tools/assets/heroClips.ts (how they move): 49 frames in 8 clips, every pixel of every frame a pixel of the user's drawings, moved and never drawn, recoloured or smoothed (a rigid, smooth warp bends the body, the head, the antennae, the legs; the blade of the sword is a rigid piece that turns about its hilt). 10 more clip(s) were drawn by hand and handed over (walk, crouch, crouchWalk, dash, attack2, aerialAttack, crouchAttack, death, drink, interact): their frames and their entry here are the artist's, and `npm run assets:animate` leaves them alone. 0 clips are STAND-INS (tag \"stand-in\"): the motion is real but the sheet has no drawing of their action, so the drawing of another one is what moves — . `npm run assets:missing` counts them as NOT delivered. Hand over drawn frames for a clip and the stand-in goes away.",
